<DocsLayout title="Agno guide | dotfetch" description="Integrate dotfetch with Agno: one agent that re-selects tools for every run, failed tool results the model can read, approval through requires_confirmation, and the RunContext.">
  <p class="eyebrow">Framework guide</p>
  <h1>Agno</h1>
  <p class="lead">dotfetch plugs into Agno's own mechanisms: a callable <code>tools</code> factory that picks each run's tools, failed tool results for errors, <code>requires_confirmation</code> for human approval, and the <code>RunContext</code> for your run state.</p>
  <p><a class="pill" href="/Agent-Gantry/docs/frameworks/agno/advanced/">Advanced Agno usage →</a></p>

  <h2>Install</h2>
  <CodeBlock lang="bash" code={`uv add "dotfetch[agno]"   # agno >= 2.6.10`} />

  <h2>Basic page: tools picked every run</h2>
  <CodeBlock lang="python" code={`from dotfetch import DotFetch
from dotfetch.agno import AgnoAdapter
from agno.models.openai import OpenAIChat

fetcher = DotFetch()

@fetcher.register(examples=["where is my order", "has order 4471 shipped"])
def get_order_status(order_id: str) -> str:
    """Return the current shipping status for an order."""
    return "in_transit"

await fetcher.sync()
agent = AgnoAdapter(fetcher).agent(model=OpenAIChat(id="gpt-5.5"), limit=5)
run = await agent.arun("Has order 4471 shipped?")     # agent.run(...) works too`} />
  <p>For a fixed set, pass <code>Agent(tools=await adapter.select(query))</code> instead.</p>

  <h2>What the model sees when a tool fails</h2>
  <p>A failed call raises <code>AgnoToolError</code>, which Agno records as the tool's failed result (<code>tool_call_error=True</code>) with the text <code>"&lt;type&gt;: &lt;message&gt;"</code>, capped at 2,000 characters, so the model can correct a bad argument or try something else.</p>
  <div class="callout"><strong>Redact or opt out:</strong> <code>AgnoAdapter(fetcher, error_formatter=redact)</code> rewrites the text; <code>error_mode="raise"</code> raises the plain <code>ToolExecutionError</code> instead.</div>

  <h2>Reading run state from a dotfetch tool</h2>
  <CodeBlock lang="python" code={`from dotfetch.agno import current_run_context

@fetcher.register
def get_balance(account: str) -> str:
    """Fetch an account balance for the signed-in user."""
    ctx = current_run_context()            # Agno RunContext, or None outside a run
    return ctx.dependencies["bank"].balance(ctx.user_id, account)

# await agent.arun("What's my balance?", user_id="dan", dependencies={"bank": bank})`} />
